# 2. Secured and Monitored Web Infrastructure

## 1. User Request Journey & Diagram

When a user wants to access `www.foobar.com`:
1. The user types `https://www.foobar.com` into their web browser.
2. The browser requests a DNS server to resolve `www.foobar.com` into IP address `8.8.8.8`.
3. The DNS server responds with IP `8.8.8.8`.
4. The client browser initiates an encrypted HTTPS connection (Port 443) to the Load Balancer (HAproxy).
5. Firewall 1 on Server 1 inspects and allows incoming traffic on Port 443.
6. HAproxy terminates SSL (decrypts traffic) and routes the HTTP request to Server 2 or Server 3 over the internal network.
7. Firewall 2 or 3 allows incoming internal HTTP traffic on Port 80 to the Web Server (Nginx).
8. The Application Server processes dynamic logic, querying MySQL Primary (writes) or MySQL Replica (reads).
9. Monitoring Clients on each server continuously collect metrics/logs and stream data to a central Monitoring Service.

